<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34b55c55097fde049c9dc6206180084f9757448ac72afb4bb497ec8b377df875</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian PM Mark Carney discusses talks with the EU, overdependence on the US and how to deal with Donald Trump in a DW interview.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:264c25ede4f9dd1beb818ad1785c08e30497e2bcfbf1e1aa9dca91f33a081589</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-do/a-79811469--a55bfac7d94c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-donald-trump-in-a-dw-interview/a-79811469?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Mark Carney tells DW that Canada is seeking closer EU ties to "diversify and deepen" partnerships beyond the Americas. Despite German pushback, he said he favors the all-new term "associate membership."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling, power, profit: Irregular migration out of eastern Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b196ecd45f0efe31de40e8b402efe04b92f62d2e7a09dfbaa468040d0d0ad3b</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-s/a-79808822--583a8979ee7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-power-profit-irregular-migration-out-of-eastern-libya/a-79808822?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">There is currently more irregular migration between eastern Libya and Crete, Greece. It's raising questions as to what connects people smugglers with powerful militias in eastern Libya and then in turn, Europeans.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fefe52406154beb62e5dbc9d8dba80c590486b53cbc5ce751c3a8c0fa807aa1d</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Seoul fears being sidelined as US reaches out to North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93ad0e0d0e0670bba0745d4de734ce4d81a116f92584903cdf0d560293dfb885</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098--b371be6c550b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With ties between South Korea and the Trump administration strained, the South Korean government worries that Donald Trump's pursuit of a diplomatic breakthrough with Kim Jong Un may come at Seoul's expense.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65d4a05de920eb585bcd21eccfda42c5968d707efdb7d6dd5585d71dcdc947c7</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India increases growth forecast for fiscal year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02ed1e9ec79d1f9d4aa4771bdcb7264fc85d94c7f8c1984fe907130109f6e17a</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971--fa1e5ffdabbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Ministry of Finance has increased its growth forecasts for the current fiscal year. But it also warned about inflation, particularly for fuel and energy, amid continued instability in the Middle East.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China leaders demand more loyalty and more initiative</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b17177d009eb7aa92446b27102711071dabc9e61d8d4dc6b3d26aacd78417361</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-leaders-demand-more-loyalty-and-more-initiative/a-79799138--290c6fd05de3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-leaders-demand-more-loyalty-and-more-initiative/a-79799138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The CCP session emphasized internal discipline, as expected, but left the question of Xi Jinping's successor unanswered. The party seems anxious of any instability as geopolitics heats up and China's economy cools down.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Human trafficking victims stranded in Guinea-Bissau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c04147ecd951e665dd57c764e38c2b2a6c06b817b7f0cf5df2baf80cee43c9e</id><updated>2026-10-31T14:36:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558--af9688fcc3e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of West Africans lured to Guinea-Bissau with promises of jobs and migration to Europe say they were exploited by a suspected trafficking network. Now many cannot afford to return home.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
